& [ConceptualModel] is one typed comparison fact
  + a ReconciliationPlan identifies one pure operation request
  + a DigestCarrier is a complete prerequisite output with retained canonical sequence and lineage
  + a DigestPair has exactly one left and one right DigestCarrier
  + CurrentRederivation proves each supplied DigestCarrier matches present prerequisite semantics
  + CommonScope is the intersection established only by exact equality of declared scope values
  + Disposition is Equal or Different over the two comparable canonical sequence identities
  + ReconciliationResult owns the plan, pair, common scope, and disposition
  + ReconciliationFault explains why no complete result exists

& [DataIdentities] are distinct
  + [operation_identity] is nonzero reconciliation_identity plus exact reconciliation profile
  + [left_operand_identity] is the complete left digest carrier value
  + [right_operand_identity] is the complete right digest carrier value
  + [digest_transform_identity] is cantor-windows-supplied-ordered-topology-inventory-digest/0.1
  + [encoding_identity] is cantor-ordered-topology-observation-encoding/0.1
  + [sequence_identity] is encoding identity plus ordered_inventory_sha256 under ordinary SHA-256 collision assumptions
  + [capability_scope_identity] is exact complete TopologyScanLimits
  + [root_scope_identity] is empty relative path plus Directory kind plus volume serial plus 16-byte file identity
  + [common_scope_identity] is encoding, capability, and root scope identity together
  + [disposition_identity] is the named Equal or Different relation for the retained operand order
  + [lineage_identity] includes every retained lower plan, correlation, carrier, and evidence record
  - never: substitute one identity because another uses the same integer, string, digest, or nested object

& [LogicalRecords] are closed
  + ReconciliationPlan contains profile and reconciliation_identity
  + DigestPair contains left and right complete WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigest values
  + CommonScope contains encoding_profile, limits, root_relative_path, root_kind, root_volume_serial, and root_file_id
  + ReconciliationDisposition is Equal or Different
  + ReconciliationResult contains result profile, plan, left, right, common_scope, and disposition
  + ReconciliationFault contains code, optional side, optional nested digest fault, field, and message
  + no timestamp, nonce, deadline, expected result, path handle, process, receipt, or admission record exists

& [OwnershipModel] is explicit
  + caller owns plan bytes and two complete carriers before invocation
  + decoder creates one bounded ReconciliationPlan
  + transform borrows plan and carriers during validation and cloning
  + current rederivation owns clones of each prerequisite plan and assembly and consumes those clones
  + original left and right carriers remain owned by transform until success
  + success moves plan, left, right, common scope, and disposition into one result
  + failure drops all temporary clones and releases only a bounded fault
  + result getters lend immutable references and never transfer mutable authority

& [Cardinality] is exact
  + one invocation has exactly one plan
  + one invocation has exactly one left and one right operand
  + each operand has exactly one retained digest plan and one retained assembly
  + each assembly has one or more bounded members under prerequisite authority
  + exactly one root is first in each assembly
  + successful scope has exactly one encoding profile, limits value, root path, root kind, volume serial, and file ID
  + successful result has exactly one disposition
  + fault has zero or one side and zero or one nested digest fault under an exact relation

& [Relations] are explicit
  + plan correlates result but never decides disposition
  + left rederives from a clone of left.plan and left.assembly
  + right rederives from a clone of right.plan and right.assembly
  + each rederived value must equal its complete source operand
  + common profile derives from exact equality to current constants on both sides
  + common limits derives from exact left-right equality
  + common root scope derives from exact structural and strong identity equality
  + disposition derives from exact left-right digest value equality or inequality
  + result contains both original operands regardless of disposition
  + future physical wrapper may contain this result but this result never contains future physical state

& [TransformPipeline] is deterministic
  + bound encoded plan bytes
  + strictly decode plan
  + validate plan profile and nonzero identity
  + current-rederive left and require complete equality
  + current-rederive right and require complete equality
  + validate current profiles in deterministic field order
  + compare complete limits
  + extract and validate left root scope
  + extract and validate right root scope
  + compare root volume serial and file ID
  + construct one CommonScope from exact common values
  + compare digest strings and select one disposition
  + move all owned values into one result
  + any failure terminates before all later transitions

& [StateMachine] is finite and single pass
  + [EncodedPlan] transitions to DecodedPlan or Fault
  + [DecodedPlan] transitions to LeftRederived or Fault
  + [LeftRederived] transitions to RightRederived or Fault
  + [RightRederived] transitions to ProfilesComparable or Fault
  + [ProfilesComparable] transitions to LimitsComparable or Fault
  + [LimitsComparable] transitions to RootComparable or Fault
  + [RootComparable] transitions to DispositionSelected or Fault
  + [DispositionSelected] transitions to Released exactly once
  + Fault and Released are terminal
  + no retry, repair, partial release, persistence, or resumable state exists

& [ComparisonModel] keeps two equality domains separate
  + complete rederivation equality compares each carrier with its own fresh derived reproduction
  + scope equality compares selected profile, limits, and root identity values across operands
  + sequence equality compares only validated digest values across operands
  + correlation and lineage equality is neither required nor inferred across operands
  + Different is a positive state transition, not exceptional control flow

& [FaultRelations] are normalized
  + Json, Profile, ReconciliationIdentity, ScopeProfile, Limits, RootScope, Resource, and Internal have no side and no nested fault
  + LeftDigest has side Left and exactly one nested digest fault
  + RightDigest has side Right and exactly one nested digest fault
  + no other combination is valid
  + field and message scalar limits are enforced at construction
  + fault payload cannot contain plan, operand, digest value, scope, observation, carrier, or partial result

& [PhysicalRepresentation] is bounded in-memory safe Rust
  + plan input is at most 4096 bytes
  + plan is one owned String and one u64 after decode
  + two prerequisite carriers are already bounded by signed TopologyScanLimits
  + current rederivation clones at most one operand's retained plan and assembly at a time if implementation chooses sequential temporary release
  + common root file ID remains validated lowercase text in the result; no duplicate decoder is required
  + disposition is one closed enum
  + no canonical byte buffer, additional digest, map, set, filesystem object, handle, pointer, database row, or persistent state is created

& [SerializationModel] is inspectable but not constructive
  + plan and faults support strict Deserialize where caller or machine input requires it
  + disposition, common scope, and result support Serialize
  + result and common scope do not support Deserialize or Default
  + serialized result retains left before right exactly
  + serialization is evidence presentation and never the equality algorithm
  + repeated structurally equal inputs yield byte-equivalent JSON under the same serde implementation and field order

& [ProvenanceModel] is layered
  + prerequisite output-only type proves construction route, not physical origin
  + current rederivation proves present pure semantic reproduction, not fresh observation
  + common scope proves supplied comparison compatibility, not physical continuity
  + disposition proves supplied canonical sequence relation, not time relation
  + complete retained lineage permits downstream inspection without increasing evidence grade
  + future physical acquisition, completeness, time order, quiescence, receipt, and admission each require new independent provenance edges

& [ResourceModel] is inherited and explicit
  + plan byte budget is local
  + operand members, paths, streams, and bytes inherit prerequisite TopologyScanLimits
  + cloning cost is bounded by those limits and is accepted because complete rederivation is mandatory
  + no caller-configured elapsed budget exists because no clock authority exists
  + no unbounded diagnostic formatting, recursive traversal beyond bounded carriers, or whole-corpus allocation exists

& [CompatibilityModel] is fail closed
  + exact string profiles reject older, newer, or alias values
  + prerequisite canonical hash or signature drift invalidates SJS authority before compilation trust
  + Rust type or getter drift produces compile failure rather than implicit reinterpretation
  + TopologyScanLimits field growth enters complete Eq automatically but still requires signature and static review
  + no schema migration, default, lossy projection, or compatibility shim exists

& [DataQualityRules] are testable
  + every accepted plan has exact profile and nonzero identity
  + every released operand exactly rederives
  + every released common scope equals both operand scope values
  + every Equal result has equal digest values
  + every Different result has unequal digest values
  + every result retains input order and complete values
  + every fault satisfies code-side-nested cardinality
  + no result or field names a temporal or physical grade

& [DataRisks] are controlled
  + root scope underselection is controlled by four explicit fields
  + root content overclassification is controlled by excluding mutable committed fields from scope
  + limit mismatch laundering is controlled by complete Eq
  + stale semantic carrier risk is controlled by current complete rederivation
  + detached disposition risk is controlled by owned lineage
  + evidence-language inflation is controlled by closed public vocabulary and static checks

& [DataDesignGate] passes
  + identity is explicit and role separated
  + ownership and mutation are explicit
  + cardinality and ordering are explicit
  + containment and derivation relations are explicit
  + state and fault transitions are finite
  + physical representation and resource bounds are explicit
  + provenance grades and nonclaims are explicit
  + compatibility and rollback behavior are explicit
  + [source_revision_required] is false
  + [unresolved_data_question] is none inside the selected slice
  + [implementation_authority] is absent pending canonical authority
